 # Hardware/Implementation Optimization
 ## Overview
-Hardware/Implementation Optimization adapts Digital Differential Analyzer (DDA) ray traversal algorithms for execution on parallel hardware, primarily GPUs [G]. It solves performance bottlenecks of naive ray marching, such as branch divergence, memory latency, and low shader occupancy, by restructuring data layouts, unifying control flow, and optimizing register usage [G]. This family focuses on low-level execution characteristics (warps, registers, cache lines) rather than mathematical traversal logic, distinguishing it from algorithmic variants like [Parallel 3D-DDA](6247-parallel-3d-dda.md) and [GPU Screen-Space Ray Tracing via DDA](10121-gpu-screen-space-ray-tracing-via-dda.md).
+Hardware/Implementation Optimization adapts Digital Differential Analyzer (DDA) ray traversal algorithms for execution on parallel hardware, primarily GPUs [G]. It solves performance bottlenecks of naive ray marching, such as branch divergence, memory latency, and low shader occupancy, by restructuring data layouts, unifying control flow, and optimizing register usage [G]. This family focuses on low-level execution characteristics (warps, registers, cache lines) rather than mathematical traversal logic, distinguishing it from algorithmic variants like [Parallel 3D-DDA](6247-parallel-3d-dda.md) and [GPU Screen-Space Ray Tracing via DDA](10121-gpu-screen-space-ray-tracing-via-dda.md) [G].
 ## Shared principles
-1. **Branch Unification:** Divergent branches from different ray quadrants or entry points are eliminated to maintain SIMD efficiency, typically by permuting axes or unifying logic so all threads in a warp execute the same instruction stream [G].
-2. **Memory Coalescing and Caching:** Global memory access patterns are coalesced, often using Structure of Arrays (SoA) layouts for ray data and caching voxel tiles in shared memory for threads accessing nearby voxels [G].
-3. **Occupancy Management:** Shader occupancy is critical; high register allocation and excessive state carried across loops reduce concurrent warps and cause memory stalls. Optimizations reduce register pressure and deduplicate calculations [G].
-4. **Implicit Clipping:** Expensive explicit clipping is avoided by structuring tests so out-of-bounds accesses return sentinel values (e.g., zero depth) that naturally terminate iteration [G].
